FORK MODIFICATIONS (haotool/open-code-review-delegate)
================================================================================

This fork substantially modifies the upstream project. Major changes include:

1. DELIVERY MODEL
   - Ships `ocr-delegate` binary only (deterministic file selection + rule resolution)
   - Removed npm wrapper, prebuilt binary download chain, install scripts, and auto-updater
   - Source-first distribution; no prebuilt binaries published

2. SECURITY HARDENING
   - Zero outbound network capability in delivered binary
   - Dependency closure excludes LLM providers, telemetry, MCP, viewer, and session modules
   - Removed upstream GitHub Action and associated CI workflows
   - Four-gate CI guard (build, test, closure check, string scan)

3. DELEGATION ARCHITECTURE
   - Host AI agent performs review using its own subscription LLM
   - `ocr-delegate` provides deterministic engineering only
   - Skill-based workflow (skills/open-code-review/SKILL.md) replaces npm plugin distribution

4. TESTING
   - 26-scenario golden equivalence suite for delegate CLI
   - Adversarial regression fixture library (T7/T9)
   - End-to-end dry-run verification script (test/e2e/)

5. DOCUMENTATION
   - README rewritten for fork positioning and Apache-2.0 compliance
   - SECURITY.md documents fork-specific threat model
   - Multilingual README/CONTRIBUTING variants rewritten with fork disclaimers (upstream product descriptions retained only where marked upstream-only)

This is NOT an official Alibaba product. Alibaba trademarks are not used
and no official endorsement is implied.

Go module path remains `github.com/alibaba/open-code-review` to preserve
import compatibility with upstream package structure. This is a deliberate
decision documented in release notes; changing the module path would break
all internal import paths and require a full rename with no user benefit
for a source-first fork where consumers build from this repository directly.
